  "tagline": "The Java search library at the heart of Elasticsearch, OpenSearch and Solr, now with HNSW vectors.",
  "description": "Lucene is the Apache Software Foundation's Java library for inverted-index search, first written by Doug Cutting in 1999 and still the engine inside Elasticsearch, OpenSearch and Solr. It provides analyzers, BM25 and other similarities, points for numeric and geo data, doc values for sorting and aggregations, and since 9.0 HNSW vector indexes with scalar and binary quantization. Lucene 10 brought better concurrency and I/O, and the 10.5 line continues to improve vector and query performance. Use it directly when you need search embedded in a JVM application with full control; otherwise use one of the servers built on it.",
